# Workflow: artefact-ready [v2]

How to manage artefact packages using artefact-ready facility

## 2. Instructions
- Complete part or full of DAG (defined by pseudo makefile, do not run with `make` tool) to meet user intent
- If target got failure, hold execution of its parent target. Instead make sure all of its dependency targets completed

## Inventory Directory

| OS Context | Path                            |
| ---------- | ------------------------------- |
| Windows    | `~/echo-home/windows`           |
| Mac OS     | `~/echo-home/workstation/macos` |
| Linux      | `~/echo-home`                   |

## Workflow 

```Makefile
inventory:
    # Description: check if <package> exists in inventory
    # Command: `cd <inventory_path>; cat .properd/artefacts.yaml | grep <package>`
    # Success: output show `package` name
    # Failure: output show no `package` name, workflow can be aborted immediately
    # Output: <package_name> , <package_version>

download: inventory
    # Description: download package
    # Command: `.function/artefact-geti <package>`
    # Success: no error found in output
    # Failure: error found in output 
    # Input: <package_name>
    # Retry: once only

update_version: inventory
    # Description: update new version for a specific package
    # Command: `artefact-version <package_name> <new_version>`
    # Success: output `Updated`
    # Failure: error found in output 
    # Input: <package_name>, <new_version>
    # Retry: once only

register_checksum: download
    # Description: append sha256sum entries in `.properd/artefact.sha256sum` when new version of package is updated
    # Command: `artefact-256sum <package_name>`
    # Success: output with `[Entry appended]`
    # Failure: you might have to run download to make package available at local

check_sum: inventory download
    # Description: verify package integrity 
    # Command: `.function/artefacts <package_name>`
    # Success: output with `<package_name>-<package_version>.*: OK`
    # Failure: output without `<package_name>-<package_version>.*: OK`
deploy: check_sum
    # Description: install package into system
    # Command: `.function/artefact-readi <package>`
    # Success: no error found in output
    # Failure: error found in output
    # Input: check_sum must be OK and match current version found in inventory
```
